Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,There are women who never had the chance to sit in a classroom...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,...yet, somehow, they understood the power of education better than anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They woke up before the sun, worked with tired hands...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.50,0:00:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,...and carried dreams that were bigger than their own lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.00,0:00:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They watched the school gates from the outside...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.00,0:00:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They might not have known the answers to our homework...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.50,0:00:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,...but they always knew one thing: we had to keep learning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.50,0:00:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,With every quiet whisper to stay awake, they gave us wings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.00,0:00:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, we are living the dreams they never had the opportunity to pursue.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.00,0:01:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Every page we read, every door we open carries their sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.00,0:01:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They may never have called themselves teachers. But they were our first teachers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.00,0:01:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And their wisdom will live through generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.00,0:01:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Made with AI • Dedicated to our mothers • የእናቶቻችን ጥበብ
